-construction","plural","subjunctive","subjunctive-ii","third-person"],"source":"conjugation"}],"inflection_templates":[{"name":"de-conj","args":{}}],"derived":[{"word":"belieben"},{"word":"verlieben"},{"word":"Lieben"},{"word":"Liebling"}],"related":[{"word":"lieb"},{"tags":["feminine"],"word":"Liebe"},{"word":"liebenswert"},{"word":"liebenswürdig"},{"word":"liebhaben"}],"etymology_number":"1","etymology_text":"Formally from Middle High German lieben, alteration (based on liep) of rarer liuben (“to make or be dear, to treat in a friendly way”), from Old High German liuben, equivalent to lieb + -en.\nThe singularly attested Old High German liobōn (“to love”) probably remained without continuation; the modern sense was derived in late Middle High German from the noun liebe (“love”) on the model of minnen (“to love”), from minne, which had developed a sexual overtone. It remained absent from most traditional dialects, which use variants of lieb haben or gern haben instead (compare the usage note below). Cognate with Alemannic German liebe. Related to English love. Compare Dutch lieven.","etymology_links":[["lieben","lieben#Middle_High_German"],["liep","liep#Middle_High_German"],["liuben","liuben#Middle_High_German"],["liuben","liuben#Old_High_German"],["lieb","lieb#German"],["-en","-en#German"],["liobōn","liobon#Old_High_German"],["liebe","liebe#German"],["minnen","minnen#Middle_High_German"],["minne","minne#Middle_High_German"],["lieb haben","lieb haben#German"],["gern haben","gern haben#German"],["liebe","liebe#Alemannic_German"],["love","love#English"],["lieven","lieven#Dutch"]],"etymology_templates":[{"name":"root","args":{"1":"de","2":"ine-pro","3":"*lewbʰ-","id":"love"},"expansion":""},{"name":"inh","args":{"1":"de","2":"gmh","3":"lieben"},"expansion":"Middle High German lieben"},{"name":"inh","args":{"1":"de","2":"goh","3":"liuben"},"expansion":"Old High German liuben"},{"name":"suffix","args":{"1":"de","2":"lieb","3":"en"},"expansion":"lieb + -en"},{"name":"m+","args":{"1":"goh","2":"liobōn","t":"to love"},"expansion":"Old High German liobōn (“to love”)"},{"name":"cog","args":{"1":"gsw","2":"liebe"},"expansion":"Alemannic German liebe"},{"name":"cog","args":{"1":"en","2":"love"},"expansion":"English love"},{"name":"cog","args":{"1":"nl","2":"lieven"},"expansion":"Dutch lieven"}],"sounds":[{"ipa":"/ˈliːbən/"},{"ipa":"[ˈliːbən]"},{"ipa":"[ˈliːbm̩]"},{"audio":"De-lieben2.ogg","text":"Audio","ogg_url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6d/De-lieben2.ogg","mp3_url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/6d/De-lieben2.ogg/De-lieben2.ogg.mp3"},{"audio":"De-lieben.ogg","text":"Audio","ogg_url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/52/De-lieben.ogg","mp3_url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/52/De-lieben.ogg/De-lieben.ogg.mp3"},{"homophone":"liebem (some speakers)"},{"rhymes":"-iːbən"}],"hyphenations":[{"parts":["lie","ben"]}],"word":"lieben","lang":"German","lang_code":"de"}}